Z||000000||turbo86se||03-02-2000||09:40 AM||||<BR>Finally, after two and a half long weeks of having this cradleless/engineless 84 coupe sitting in my driveway with only the two front wheels, I finally got it towed out of here! Now I can get my 86SE out of the garage. It served its purpose, I removed the entire enterior, all exterior panels except for rear clip, which was cracked! This was going to be my project car for the summer, but it would need a lot of work, and while I was removing panels, I could see more and more evidence of a wreck underneath the front. The radiator was in bad shape, and everything underneath was pretty mangled. I now have 3 '84 fascias, a pair of p/w/l/m doors, 7 fenders, tail-lights, a hood, sunroof glass, 2 dashes, carpet and many other parts in storage. Later today I'm going to meet with someone in Conway who has parts he's giving away. I'm also interested in checking out his Quad-4 conversion. If anyone needs anything, LMK!<BR>thanks for the space!!  -joel||||reg||10
